{
  "_readme": [
    "Which source model backs each logical biome prop. Consumed by scripts/build-biome-atlas.mjs.",
    "",
    "`nodes` are source mesh node names. Omit it to take every mesh node in the file.",
    "To find them: docs/BIOME_LIBRARY_INDEX.json, field glb.meshNodeNames. Rebuild that",
    "index with `pnpm assets:index-biome-library`.",
    "",
    "`targetHeight` is the authored world height in metres — one world unit is one metre.",
    "The builder measures the selected geometry and derives scale from it; nothing is",
    "inferred from the source file's unit setting. `sink` (metres) pushes a prop below",
    "y=0 for props that should bed into the ground.",
    "",
    "`maxTriangles` is the budget for the whole prop. These are instanced scatter props,",
    "so the budget is what keeps a hundred of them affordable, not the file size.",
    "",
    "Licence: the builder refuses to write an unapproved prop into public/models —",
    "use --draft to inspect one first. A new entry starts `pending`; record evidence",
    "in CREDITS.md before flipping it to `approved`."
  ],

  "sourceRoots": {
    "world": "~/Desktop/world build",
    "animals": "~/Desktop/3d models animals"
  },

  "out": "biomes",

